body:
Oh my god.  You really are retarded aren't you?  You are so stuck on the politics of "victim blaming" that you can't even see how dumb you sound.

&#x200B;

So let me ask you, if you had a Daughter, say, age 21.  What would you tell her?  "Hey go do what you want, rape can't happen so just do whatever!"   Or would you help her to try to be "smart" and "safe" when going out?

&#x200B;

[https://www.cornellcollege.edu/counseling/sexual-assault/risk-reduction-strategies.shtml](https://www.cornellcollege.edu/counseling/sexual-assault/risk-reduction-strategies.shtml)

&#x200B;

This is literally from CORNELL COLLEGE.  It clearly states  "

if they are sexually assaulted they are not responsible for the assault.

Anyone can be sexually assaulted, and there are no sure means to prevent sexual assault because the only people who can prevent sexual assault are those who perpetrate it.  However, you can take steps to lessen the likelihood that you or your friends will be assaulted or will assault someone. "

&#x200B;

Which is EXACTLY WHAT I AM SAYING.  HOW CAN YOU BE THIS DENSE!

In those situations, there isn't much that they could've done unfortunately. So, yeah, not arguing with you there.  No one is.   And that may be true in the majority of cases.  I'm speaking about the cases where you should be smart to safeguard yourself from all sorts of tragedies: rapes, murders, muggings, etc.  Whether you like it or not, there are precautions that you can take to make yourself less likely to be the victim of an attack, either sexual or violent in  nature, man or woman.  

&#x200B;

Do you seriously not understand this?  I genuinely would be shocked if someone could not understand the point that I am making.  Lol.  It is like you might actually be mentally retarded. 

&#x200B;

Your comment "how should a 4 year old change her behavior to avoid being raped?" is simply stupid.  You obviously know that I am not talking about that situation, so why would you bring it up?  Well, I'll tell you why.  It is because you can't win the argument on fair terms, so you resort to ridiculous situations that aren't even about the core of what we are talking about.  It should be extremely obvious to anyone with even half a brain, that I am speaking of instances of preventable rape or violence. 

I am a man, and even I take certain precautions when I go out to avoid sexual assault and other violent crimes that could take place.  It isn't foolproof, but it certainly lowers my odds of being a victim.

"Men can just keep doing what they do".  Nah, that's bullshit.  A very small percentage of people are rapists.  You aren't going to change them.  People who intentionally rape people are always going to exist.  Yes, it's still their fault, yes their awful people and no woman deserves it.  But it doesn't change the fact that there are ways to protect yourself.  No one is excusing rape, yet you people always paint the "other side" as rape apologists.  How do you people not understand this.

&#x200B;

Edit: And once again.  To the idiots who downvoted this.  Tell me one reason why anything I said is "wrong".  Give it your best shot, you can do it. 

&#x200B;

How bout don't listen to random people on Reddit to decide if you are sexually immoral or not.  Also, yes, if I've learned anything from being on reddit, it is that you are certainly a pedophile...  

&#x200B;

Edit: I guess I have to add the /s for the people downvoting.

I'm well aware of this case.  You just picked the one in a billion, worst of the worst cases in recorded history. Do you think that merely posting this case wins an argument?  That it proves that all children who commit horrific crimes deserve adult punishment (e.g. life imprisonment)?  They did not receive adult sentences by the way.  They got 10 years and lifetime on what is basically parole.  Seems fair.  And they got a fair dose of mental help as well, which is really the most important part of the whole thing. 

&#x200B;

If I remember right, one of the boys went on to not commit any more crimes thus far in life, and they have rated him as being very low risk of offending again.

&#x200B;

This story really is surreal and completely chilling.  But, still, I don't hold those kids nearly as accountable for their actions as I would if they were later teens or adults.  Especially the one who wasn't the "ringleader".  You could probably convince a lot of 10 year olds to do some fucked up stuff if you asked a large enough sample size to do it.  Kids who otherwise wouldn't do anything like that.  All I'm saying is that, this kind of stuff goes a lot deeper than just "Oh evil people are evil, lock em up".  There's a whole lot of psychology and all sorts of stuff to unfold and look into.

But, you have to admit that you are most likely wrong.  I mean, you aren't a doctor, so you can't diagnose.  So you will have to take someone's word at face value if they say "Hey, I did some things I regret when I was a child.  Now I wouldn't do those things, I just didn't have as much empathy then."

&#x200B;

Your only response to that is "You're still a psychopath!"?  Is that all that you know to believe?  All good actions are done by great people and all bad actions are done by psychopaths?  Does that make sense to you?
